{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## CORRECTION: change 2271 was NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT. This ticket is not fixed.\n\nI wrote that 2271 fixes the attested gates, pending only deployment. It is deployed, and they\nstill fail. Correcting that here rather than letting the earlier comment stand.\n\n### What 2271 did achieve — verified on the live container\n\n    REBAR_ROOT=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code\n    MCP_CODE_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code\n    git -C /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code rev-parse origin/main\n      -> 269f7b49c44fd87da2bf26f8f5d35ba6d9df6ad0\n    git -C /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code rev-parse main   -> same\n    origin -> https://github.com/navapbc/rebar.git [blob:none]\n\nThe repository is provisioned, healthy, and resolves BOTH refs. That half of the diagnosis was\nright and the fix works.\n\n### The remaining cause: the snapshot layer never consults REBAR_ROOT\n\n`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:264` (and identically at `:503` and `:699`):\n\n    root = str(repo_root) if repo_root else \".\"\n\nWhen `repo_root` is `None` it falls back to the literal `\".\"` — the PROCESS CWD, which is\n`/app` in the container, and `/app` has no object DB because `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`.\nIt never asks the config layer.\n\nAnd none of the MCP LLM tools pass a `repo_root`: `_mcp_llm.py:116` (`review_code`), `:146`\n(`scan_spec`), `:196` (`verify_completion`) all call `rebar.llm.*` without one. So every\nattested-source tool takes the `None` -> `\".\"` path.\n\nDemonstrated directly, from a non-repo cwd with REBAR_ROOT set:\n\n    repo_root_or_none()  -> /Users/joeoakhart/71e7-codex-mcp-pat   (honours it correctly)\n    snapshot default     -> \".\"                                    (ignores it)\n\n### The experiment that settles it — and refutes the reported cause\n\nA parallel Copilot session retried `review_plan` with an EXPLICIT full SHA and got the same\nerror: `cannot resolve ref '269f7b49c44fd87da2bf26f8f5d35ba6d9df6ad0' to a commit in '.'`. It\nconcluded the server's clone is 'stale, disconnected, or configured differently'.\n\nThat conclusion is WRONG, and the SHA is what disproves it: it is exactly the commit I verified\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code` resolves. A stale clone cannot explain failing to find a commit the\nclone demonstrably contains. Looking in the WRONG DIRECTORY explains it exactly — and the error\nmessage names that directory, `'.'`, not `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`. The `'.'` was the tell all\nalong.\n\n### Class\n\nSame family as `damageable-huge-xiphosuran`: shipped code bypassing rebar's own configured\nresolver and substituting a hardcoded default. That one is `tracker_dir`; this is `repo_root`.\n\nThis ticket stays IN PROGRESS. AC1-AC3 remain unticked, correctly."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787859682124446001,"uuid":"7a825e60-c311-4461-8bd6-5c97319bc86a"}